4. Public vs Private Subnets

Feature	Public Subnet	Private Subnet
Route to Internet Gateway	Usually present	No direct internet route
Publicly reachable resources	Possible, if addressing and security allow	Not directly through an IGW
Common workloads	Public load balancers and web servers	Application servers and databases
Outbound internet access	Through an IGW when configured	Often through a NAT Gateway for IPv4
Security	Restrict access carefully	Keep internal workloads isolated

Remember: Public and private are networking classifications based on routing and reachability, not simply whether a subnet has a public IP address assigned.

