9. VPC Security Best Practices

1. Keep databases in private subnets.
2. Avoid exposing application servers directly to the public internet unless necessary.
3. Restrict inbound Security Group rules to trusted sources and required ports.
4. Avoid unrestricted SSH or RDP access.
5. Use IAM policies with least privilege to control who can modify networking resources.
6. Use VPC Flow Logs to capture IP traffic information for monitoring and troubleshooting.
7. Use VPC Endpoints for supported AWS services when private connectivity is appropriate.
8. Plan non-overlapping CIDR blocks for VPCs and connected networks.
9. Deploy critical workloads across multiple AZs where appropriate.
10. Monitor NAT Gateway data processing and other networking charges.
11. Use Network ACLs where subnet-level allow/deny filtering is required.
12. Review route tables regularly to prevent unintended traffic paths.

