11. Important VPC Interview Questions

Q1. What is Amazon VPC?

Amazon VPC is a logically isolated virtual network in AWS that lets users control IP addressing, subnets, routing, and network security.

Q2. What is the difference between a public and a private subnet?

A public subnet has a route to an Internet Gateway. A private subnet does not have a direct route to an Internet Gateway.

Q3. What is the difference between an Internet Gateway and a NAT Gateway?

An Internet Gateway enables internet communication for appropriately configured resources. A NAT Gateway allows private IPv4 resources to initiate outbound connections without accepting unsolicited inbound connections through the NAT Gateway.

Q4. What is the difference between a Security Group and a Network ACL?

A Security Group is stateful and applies at the resource/network-interface level. A Network ACL is stateless and applies at the subnet level.

Q5. Can a VPC span multiple Availability Zones?

Yes. A VPC can span multiple Availability Zones, but each subnet belongs to only one Availability Zone.

Q6. What is a VPC Endpoint?

A VPC Endpoint provides private connectivity to supported AWS services or endpoint services without requiring a public internet route for that connection.

Q7. What is VPC Peering?

VPC Peering connects two VPCs for private IP communication, subject to routing and security configurations. It does not support transitive routing.

Q8. What is a CIDR block?

A CIDR block defines a range of IP addresses for a network or subnet.

Q9. What is VPC Flow Logs?

VPC Flow Logs capture information about IP traffic to and from network interfaces and can be published to supported destinations for analysis and troubleshooting.

Q10. Why are databases usually placed in private subnets?

Private subnets reduce direct internet exposure. Access can be restricted to authorized application components using routing and security rules.

Q11. What is the difference between VPC Peering and Transit Gateway?

VPC Peering provides point-to-point connectivity, whereas Transit Gateway acts as a central hub for connecting multiple VPCs and supported external networks.

Q12. Can two VPCs have overlapping CIDR blocks?

Overlapping CIDR blocks prevent normal VPC Peering between those VPCs. Non-overlapping address ranges are important for straightforward routing between networks.

