12. Key Takeaways

* Amazon VPC provides an isolated and configurable networking environment in AWS.
* CIDR blocks define network IP ranges.
* Subnets divide a VPC into smaller network segments.
* Route tables determine where traffic goes.
* Internet Gateways support internet routing for public resources.
* NAT Gateways provide outbound IPv4 internet access for private workloads.
* Security Groups are stateful; Network ACLs are stateless.
* VPC Endpoints support private connectivity to supported services.
* VPC Peering connects two VPCs, while Transit Gateway supports larger network architectures.
* Good VPC design combines correct routing, least-privilege security, and appropriate multi-AZ deployment.

